# Pinned `spec` revision the conformance runner validates against.
#
# The runner refuses to run if the spec checkout it is given is not at this
# commit (override with --allow-spec-drift when deliberately testing against
# unreleased vocabulary). Without a pin the suite silently tracks whatever is
# on spec `main`, so a run that passed yesterday can pass today for a
# different reason.
#
# To re-pin: check out the new spec revision, put its full SHA and its
# VOCAB_VERSIONS line below, run `make -C . conformance` (or
# `scripts/run_conformance.py`), and record the resulting counts in the PR.

# Pinned at the MERGE commit of the-cascade-protocol/spec PR #18 on `main`
# (core v3.6 / health v2.7 / clinical v1.15; tags `vocab/core-v3.6`,
# `vocab/health-v2.7`, `vocab/clinical-v1.15`). While that PR was open this
# file briefly pinned its branch commit 728f9ae -- the five new negative and
# ratchet fixtures are rejected by nothing under the previous pin (measured
# RED-first against d162f68), so pinning ahead was what made them mean
# something. Re-measured at this merge commit before merging this repo's PR:
# 109 passed / 27 known failures / 0 skipped / 136 total, unchanged from the
# branch-pin measurement.

